  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. Input 14 deliberately mentions a lantern that is not in Lyra's inventory, to test PHANTOM detection; its expected call is a plain perception check with no advantage. Input 12 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Lyra. Input 22 invites the Keeper to name a thief, who would be a phantom character. Fire Bolt (input 6) is a cantrip and spends no slot; Cure Wounds (input 13) spends one of two. Inputs 3 to 11 give more attacks than the fight usually needs: an attack on a rat that is already down, or after the encounter has ended, is rejected and does not advance the game. Whether the encounter is over by input 13 depends on the seed (docs/scenario_format.md section 5, point 2)."
